      "summary": {
        "unit_id": "hmh07-lua-follow4:037",
        "answer": "When a menu exists it registers MOUSE1 and confirm callbacks. A busy spinner suppresses simulation; otherwise the callbacks read Button/KeyShortcut when a model exists, play DefaultClip and simulate a press. Confirm returns false for an actual cross-button binding. keyPrompt adds Button-based resizing. footerTooltip adds shortcut text conversion and a KeybindMessages.isBindingKey subscription. All callback gates and returns are retained in the nested traces; installing them does not press a button. Returns immediately off PC. On PC stores __focusNavigationElementCallback; when invoked it returns activeWidget only when present and focusable, else nil. It does not select/focus a widget during installation. Walks StickyElements with ipairs and calls MigrateSingleStickyElementsBackward with the original first argument, each element and the original second argument. It does not define migrati [excerpt; exact source record identified separately]",
